\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Dynamic 72-Hour Autonomous Storm Rollout Trajectories across Contrasting Global Archetypes (Observing System Simulation Experiment).} Continuous shoreline position evolution $\Delta X(t)$ comparing Ground Truth Nature Run $x(t)$ (black) against Model A (Data-Driven, red dashed), Model B (PINN Loss-Guided, orange dotted), Model C (Feature-Guided, teal dash-dotted), and Model D (Dual-Guided, dark slate solid) centered on peak compound hazard ($t = 0$, crimson dotted line). Notice how Model B stabilizes acute shock without hallucinating fair-weather accretion during peak storm forcing ($\text  {BSS} = +0.108$), while Model C captures dynamic recovery amplitude ($r = 0.574$, reaching $r = 0.839$ at Truc Vert).}}{10}{}\protected@file@percent }
